## Primary Task: Add Split-View Minimum Size Test

Read `src/mogwser/splitview/SplitViewTree.mjs` first to understand how minimum panel size is enforced. The tree uses position calculations where each leaf gets a percentage of the container. The minimum should be 7%.

Add a new test to the END of `tests/unit/test_splitview_tree.js`:

```js
add_task(async function test_minimum_panel_size_enforcement() {
  // Create a tree with two leaves where one would be below 7%
  const tree = new SplitViewTree("row");
  tree.addLeaf("tab-1");
  tree.addLeaf("tab-2");

  // Get positions — each leaf should get at least 7% of the container
  const positions = tree.getPositions();

  for (const pos of positions) {
    const width = pos.right - pos.left;
    const height = pos.bottom - pos.top;
    Assert.ok(
      width >= 7 || height >= 7,
      `Panel dimension should be at least 7% (got width=${width}, height=${height})`
    );
  }
});
```

